~*
~*  This job builds the openings library for CHESS 4.9. The CHESS 4.9
~*  tape carries no openings book, so the program plays every opening
~*  from its own search. The CHESS 4.6 tape, however, carries the
~*  Northwestern openings book as decks W/... and B/... of its program
~*  library, written in the program's own learning-mode command language
~*  (INI, LET MSCODE, SWITCH LW/LB/NOR, and moves in descriptive
~*  notation).
~*
~*  The job copies the 4.6 program library from the tape, extracts those
~*  decks with MODIFY as one record of commands (a modset drops the *WEOR
~*  directives that would split the record and appends DUMP and END),
~*  runs CHESS 4.9 with that record as its input file so that it records
~*  every position and move in its positions library, and saves the
~*  quick-load dump of the library as CHESBK. The chess49bk.post script
~*  copies CHESBK to the LIBRARY catalog, and the CHESS procedure, which
~*  this job also refreshes in the PRODUCT file, passes it to CHESS 4.9
~*  as the openings library file.
~*
~*  Recording the book's roughly 15,000 commands takes CHESS 4.9 about
~*  ten CPU minutes, so expect this job to run for the better part of an
~*  hour. Its output lists every command as the program read it, so
~*  ILLEGAL MOVE or AMBIGUOUS MOVE lines in the job's printout identify
~*  any deck lines the program could not use.
~*
CHESSBK.
$USER,INSTALL,${../site.cfg:PASSWORDS:INSTALL:INSTALL}.
$NORERUN.
$SETTL,*.
$SETASL,*.
$SETJSL,*.
$COPYBR,INPUT,PROC.
$COPYBR,INPUT,MODS.
$ASSIGN,${2},TAPE,D=GE,LB=KL,F=I,PO=R.
$REWIND,TAPE.
$SKIPF,TAPE.
$COPY,TAPE,OPL.
$RETURN,TAPE.
$REWIND,OPL,MODS.
$MODIFY,P=OPL,C=BOOK,LO=E,I=MODS.
$REWIND,BOOK.
$GET,CHESLIB=CHESS49/UN=LIBRARY.
$LIBRARY,CHESLIB/A.
CHESS,BOOK,OUTPUT,LIBRARY.
$REWIND,CHESBK.
$REPLACE,CHESBK.
$ATTACH,PRODUCT/M=W,WB.
$LIBEDIT,P=PRODUCT,B=PROC,I=0,C.
***
*** CHESSBK COMPLETE
***
EXIT.
***
*** CHESSBK FAILED
***
~eor
~include chess.proc
~eor
*IDENT CHESBK
*/        EXTRACT THE OPENINGS BOOK DECKS FROM THE CHESS 4.6 PROGRAM
*/        LIBRARY AS ONE RECORD OF LEARNING-MODE COMMANDS FOR CHESS 4.9,
*/        ENDING WITH A QUICK-LOAD DUMP OF THE RESULTING LIBRARY.
*/        CASTLING WRITTEN WITH ZEROS IS AMBIGUOUS TO CHESS 4.9, SO THE
*/        EIGHT SUCH LINES ARE REWRITTEN WITH LETTER O.
*DECK W/BIRDS
*D W/BIRDS.1
*DECK W/RUYW
*D W/RUYW.1
*DECK W/SICIL
*D W/SICIL.1006
O-O
*D W/SICIL.1248
O-O
*D W/SICIL.1442
O-O
*D W/SICIL.1447
O-O
*D W/SICIL.1468
O-O
*D W/SICIL.1579
O-O
*DECK W/GORIN
*D W/GORIN.539
O-O
*D W/GORIN.551
O-O
*DECK B/BENON
*I B/BENON.2294
DUMP,CHESBK
END
*EDIT W/BIRDS,W/RUYW,W/RUYWO,W/PETRF,W/FRNCH,W/SICIL,W/PIRC
*EDIT W/NIMZO,W/CAROK,W/CENTR,W/ALEKN,W/GORIN
*EDIT B/BIRDS,B/SICIL,B/ENGLI,B/PETRF,B/KGA,B/CENTR,B/BENON
